course: dictionary
lesson: 959
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word blower is a good example. It can mean a machine that blows air, a person who blows something, or, in old British slang, a telephone.
explain: «Get on the blower to the plumber.» Blower does not mean a machine here. The clues are get on and plumber: you ring a plumber on the phone. So on the blower means on the phone.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Get on the telephone to the plumber» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Look at the words around the hard word first, then test your choice.
fact: Blower is a noun, so it names a thing or a person: a blower, blowers.
fact: A leaf blower is a machine that blows air, often used in autumn to move leaves.
fact: On the blower is informal, old-fashioned British slang meaning on the phone.
fact: A glass-blower shapes hot glass by blowing into it.
fact: A whistle-blower is a person who tells the public or the authorities about wrongdoing in a company or organisation.
exercise: What does blower mean in «Get on the blower to the plumber»? | A person who tells on wrongdoing | *The telephone | A machine that blows air | A glass-blower
exercise: «Snow blowers clear the paths in winter.» What is a snow blower? | A person who blows whistles at football matches | *A machine that blows snow away | A telephone | A kind of glass
exercise: Whistle-blowers speak up about wrongdoing. What is a whistle-blower? | A fan heater | *A person who tells the public about wrongdoing | A person who makes glass | A leaf blower
test: A glass-blower shapes what? | *Hot glass | Snow | Telephones | Leaves
test: Which word means a person who tells the public about wrongdoing? | Leaf blower | *Whistle-blower | Glass-blower | Fan heater
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Get on the blower to the plumber»? | A machine that blows air | *The telephone, because the plumber is someone you ring | A glass-blower | A whistle-blower
